            (the game only shows the ping icon above 100 ms), 110-140 ms across the Atlantic, more to Asia, a
            spike to 170-250 ms when the countdown starts, and packet loss in fights on a bad server. Fika
            clients show their real ping to the host instead.</p>
        <div class="fb-grid fb-grid-3">
            <label class="fb-field">
                <span class="fb-label">Your location@(Tip(
                    "Where you play from. Servers in your region give the lowest ping and are the ones you usually match "
                    + "into."))</span>
                <select @bind="simulation.World.Location">
                    @foreach (var region in PopulationStore.Regions)
                    {
                        <option value="@region">@region</option>
                    }
                </select>
            </label>
        </div>
        <div class="fb-switch-row">
            <label class="fb-switch">
                <input type="checkbox" role="switch" @bind="simulation.World.SimulateConnection"/>
                <span class="fb-switch-track"></span>
                Simulate ping and packet loss@(Tip(
                    "Show ping and packet loss from your matched server in raid, using the game's own connection icons."))
            </label>
        </div>
        <div class="fb-switch-row">
            <label class="fb-switch">
                <input type="checkbox" role="switch" @bind="simulation.World.ConnectionLossEvents"/>
                <span class="fb-switch-track"></span>
                Connection lost events@(Tip(
                    "Off by default. On a bad server, a fight can end in Server connection lost. Closing the message, or "
                    + "waiting out its timer, ends the raid as missing in action. At most once per raid, not on Fika."))
            </label>
        </div>
        <div class="fb-switch-row">
            <label class="fb-switch">
                <input type="checkbox" role="switch" @bind="simulation.World.RubberBanding"/>
                <span class="fb-switch-track"></span>
                Rubber banding@(Tip(
                    "Off by default. Right after the countdown and when a bad server drops packets, you now and then snap "
                    + "back to where you were a moment ago. Bad servers drop packets most in fights, but also in quiet "
                    + "moments. Heavy loss can hold you in place for a few seconds. When the connection is lost you freeze "
                    + "where the server last saw you. Not on Fika."))
            </label>
        </div>
        <div class="fb-switch-row">
            <label class="fb-switch">
                <input
                    type="checkbox"
                    role="switch"
                    @bind="simulation.World.RubberBandingBots"
                    disabled="@(!simulation.World.RubberBanding)"/>
                <span class="fb-switch-track"></span>
                Rubber banding affects bots@(Tip(
                    "Off by default. Needs Rubber banding. Every bot within 150 m of you snaps back on the same packet loss, "
                    + "so enemies jump around on a bad server too. Not on Fika."))
            </label>
        </div>
    </section>
    @SimulationSave
}
